      origins: "Tunkhannock 14-point Pitch is a Pennsylvania regional variant of Pitch, related to Oklahoma 10-point Pitch. It is documented as normally played cutthroat by four players but can also be played in partnership. The game takes its name from the Tunkhannock region; detailed rules were preserved on Bill and Joe's archived 14 point Tunkhannock Pitch page (2000).",
